# stacklets/core/caddy.snippet
#
# core owns its home — the bare {$STACK_DOMAIN} — and serves the
# persistent-link resolver under /go/. A dashboard / welcome page can take
# over `/` later; for now home just answers a friendly placeholder.
#
# Only /go/*, the card pages (/card, /card/*) and the dashboard
# (/dashboard, /dashboard/*, its styles included) are forwarded to the
# tools server, and to its public listener (8001), which serves them and
# nothing else, to paired devices only (tools-server/devices); the pages
# read only. Its internal listener
# (8000) serves search, logs and status to the stack's containers and must
# never be the target of a route from outside.
#
# A `handle` takes one matcher, so a page with two paths (`/card` and
# `/card/*`) gets a named matcher. Two paths on the `handle` line itself
# make Caddy refuse the whole Caddyfile, every other site included.
#
# The /go prefix mirrors core's LINK_PREFIX env (default "go"); if you move
# the namespace, change both.

{$STACK_DOMAIN} {
    handle /go/* {
        reverse_proxy stack-core-tools:8001
    }
    @cards path /card /card/*
    handle @cards {
        reverse_proxy stack-core-tools:8001
    }
    @dashboard path /dashboard /dashboard/*
    handle @dashboard {
        reverse_proxy stack-core-tools:8001
    }
    handle {
        respond "famstack — home server" 200
    }
}
